  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two long, straight, parallel wires, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span>, are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> in a vacuum. Wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> carries a current in the upward direction and wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> carries a current in the downward direction.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the nature and the dependence on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> of the magnetic force per unit length exerted by wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> on wire <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Attractive force proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{r}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\">Attractive force proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{r^2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\">Repulsive force proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{r}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\">Repulsive force proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{r^2}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
